.TH SHADOW 1
.SH NAME
shadow \- a shadow is the same model, sheared
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/shadow
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Shadow
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/Shadow.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
The shadow is not computed.  It is the model drawn a second time through
one extra matrix that flattens it onto a plane, with a lighting function
that returns black for every face, sharing the first pass's depth buffer
so it lands behind.  The original's comment on the choice of plane is
"pick one to suit your taste; it doesn't have to have a norm of 1.0", and
on the whole idea, "the shadow image b.s.  Any is plausible."
.PP
The three angles advance on seventy, ninety and a hundred and ten frames,
which share no common factor, so the tumble never repeats.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/shadow.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR draw3d (2),
.IR wm (1)
